{
  "case_id": "2022-22-58",
  "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are more than 11 million removable non-citizens in this country, and DHS has about 6,000 interior enforcement officers. To focus the agency's limited resources on threats to public safety, national security, and border security, DHS adopted enforcement priorities. But the district court issued a sweeping ruling vacating the guidelines nationwide. This Court should reverse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On the merits, the INA does not create an unyielding mandate to apprehend and remove every non-citizen described in provisions that use the term \"shall.\" This Court has repeatedly held that the word \"shall\" does not displace background principles of enforcement discretion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: General, does that same provision, 1252(f), also affect redressability for standing purposes?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Let me ask you about another case. Is it the position of the United States that the states lacked standing in the Little Sisters of the Poor case from two years ago because their expected additional healthcare spending was an indirect injury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it would be wrong to say that \"shall\" means \"shall,\" and I would -- I would welcome"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Are those --\nJUSTICE JACKSON: But --\nJUSTICE KAVANAUGH: -- are those\nbackground principles constitutional principles?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: And does this one\nGENERAL PRELOGAR: But we're not --\nJUSTICE KAVANAUGH: -- does this one\ntransgress Article II, this statute, if -- if the Chief Justice posits \"shall\" means \"shall\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The answer to that question is no, we think that the \"shall take into custody\" language has to be read against the backdrop of enforcement discretion, and it would be totally unmanageable to have a judicially enforceable duty to go out and apprehend, because how many officers do we have to put on the manhunt? How long do we have to look? How many resources do we have to devote to it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the agency has always implemented these provisions, which were added to the INA in 1996, in recognition that it retains its background principles of enforcement discretion. And so it has never implemented the statute with respect to 1226, 1231, or some of the other big ones, like 1225, that use \"shall\" as creating an inflexible mandate to -- to go after each and every one of the non-citizens described in those provisions. And that has been constant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: We haven't had a chance to discuss 1252 much, and I'd like your thoughts on that. In particular, if we were to agree with you on that, do we have to address your standing arguments, let alone the merits?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So we have never disputed that \"set aside\" can sometimes mean \"vacate.\" But I think it's equally clear that that text can sometimes bear the meaning of \"disregard\" or literally \"set to the side.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the first time we started to make them was in 2008 in the Summers versus Earth Island Institute case. We've repeated it pretty consistently since the Little Sisters case in the last administration and in cases here, and some lower courts, now that they are actually looking at our arguments, have recognized the force of those arguments."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: I'm saying that if a court lacks jurisdiction when it lacks the authority to issue a particular remedy, why wouldn't we understand the APA then -- why wouldn't we understand this issue as a matter of statutory interpretation to be jurisdictional? Because, if the district court is entertaining an action to award a particular kind of relief that it lacks authority to award, would that be jurisdictional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: We have not previously argued that this APA limit is jurisdictional. The reason we made the arguments under 1252 is because it specifically says no court shall have jurisdiction to do this, and we think that that is Congress clearly"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. I'd like to move to the merits a little bit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 100,
        "start": 100
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: How about if Congress said you must prosecute, that the executive must prosecute everyone who violates this law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Florida",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0004-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 102,
        "start": 102
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I know Florida's amicus brief says, well, the executive will then strive to meet its obligations. \"Strive to\" is not a usual term of a judicial order."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. STONE",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0004-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 102,
        "start": 102
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think, consistent with the district court's findings, that individual officers in ICE will go back to -- to not believing that their enforcement discretion has been restrained in the ways the prosecutorial -- the -- rather, the Guidelines and those have -- have caused that to be."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0005-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 104,
        "start": 104
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our argument doesn't run to removal at all, Justice Sotomayor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0005-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 104,
        "start": 104
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It runs to arrest and detention."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0005-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 105,
        "start": 105
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Answer yes or no to that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0005-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 105,
        "start": 105
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, really, this case is all about the people that a detainer has been put on and that the government can't withdraw that detainer once they put it on?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0005-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 106,
        "start": 106
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the government now have to put the resources in place to watch the prison every day to see if someone has been released?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0006-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 128,
        "start": 128
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: You might get a chance to clarify that because I completely lost the thread, and I apologize, General Stone, but are you saying that 1226(c) applies only once removal proceedings are pending?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0007-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 145,
        "start": 145
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Well, wouldn't -- wouldn't Congress have to be clear that that's what that was actually trying to do? I mean, I would think constitutional avoidance would counsel us to read their statute not to -- to even, you know, create the kind of constitutional problem you're talking about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0007-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 145,
        "start": 145
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STONE: Three points, Your Honor, the first being that this Court has held previously that exercises of detention over non-citizens can be constitutionally tolerable even when they're constitutionally intolerable against citizens."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0007-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 149,
        "start": 149
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Justice Kavanaugh, you asked what the consequences of that would be on the ground. Here's what I think it would mean. If this Court actually said that \"shall\" displaces all enforcement discretion, then DHS would be under a judicially enforceable obligation to take enforcement action against whomever it first encounters on the ground who might be subject to one of these provisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-22-58",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c736ac4497b835116006f9ba89be459f535e207f9dd7daf9a8188f55787e9de",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c736ac4497b-0007-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 152,
        "start": 152
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
